212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (The problem we address is predicting glacier melt under uncertain and variable climate conditions. Glacier melting depends on factors such as air temperature, precipitation, ice albedo, cloudiness, and snowfall threshold, all of which exhibit natural variability. Deterministic models use fixed inputs and produce a single estimate, which fails to capture uncertainty and extreme scenarios. Hence, a probabilistic approach is required to model variability and better understand the range and risk of glacier melt outcomes.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
